{
  "id": "user_task_7",
  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) UPDATE DEAL VALUES: From deal worklist `deal_worklist_wl2`, update the value of each deal that is NOT on hold (skip on_hold on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists on-hold look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then set the deal's value. Then, from worklist `record_payment_wl1`, record the settlement payment against the invoice: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) SEND QUOTES: From quote worklist `quote_worklist_wl2`, send a price quote for each deal NOT already quoted (skip quoted on its dereferenced record — the list mixes already-quoted look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and its contact record for the on-file email, then send the quote. Then, from worklist `create_task_wl1`, create the renewal follow-up task: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) WRITE OFF INVOICES: From writeoff worklist `writeoff_worklist_wl2`, write off each uncollectible invoice that is NOT disputed (skip disputed on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists disputed look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then write it off. Then, from worklist `delete_task_wl1`, delete the obsolete reconciliation task: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) CREATE DEALS: From deal-request worklist `deal_request_worklist_wl2`, create a deal for each request NOT flagged duplicate (skip duplicate on its dereferenced record — the list mixes duplicate look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then create the deal. Then, from worklist `create_invoice_wl1`, create the draft invoice for the new deal: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (E) ONBOARD LEADS: From lead worklist `lead_worklist_wl2`, onboard each inbound lead that is NOT spam (skip spam on its dereferenced record — the list mixes spam look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then create the contact. Then, from worklist `delete_deal_wl1`, delete the superseded pipeline deal: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier. One value per item is SPLIT across two records: where a record carries a `base_<field>`, the real figure is that base PLUS the matching `<field>_adjustment` held on the other record the worklist entry references.",
